WEBVTT

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:05.950
Shugo, shugo.

00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:06.960
Shugo, shugo.

00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:07.590
Shugo, shugo!

00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:10.110
Start it off with a Doki! It's Shugo Chara time!

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:13.670
This time, we meet a girl who idolizes Utau-chan.

00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:16.590
And Amu-chan is totally stressed out about it!

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:19.080
I wonder what kind of things will happen.

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:21.210
We hope you enjoy it!

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:22.310
Doki!

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:33.410
Pyon Pyon

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:34.570
Fumu Fumu

00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:35.480
Yeah! Yeah!

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:37.080
Howa Howa

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:38.280
Kira Kira

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:39.210
Yeah! Yeah!

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:41.970
What color is your egg?

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:44.750
Yeah! Yeah! Yeah!

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:49.790
Even if you say mean things,

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:53.640
I know you really love me.

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:57.310
Even if we fight a lot,

00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:00.980
it's just 'cause we're always together.

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:04.040
Because you believe in me,

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:07.800
I can do anything!

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:14.100
And that's why I unlock my heart!

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:19.810
The person you want to be; things you want to say.

00:01:19.810 --> 00:01:23.470
Important things; things that are true.

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:27.180
Who you are; what you've yet to realize.

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:30.830
Mysterious things; happy things.

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:35.740
All of these things are inside your egg!

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:39.880
Pyon Pyon

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:41.030
Fumu Fumu

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:41.970
Yeah! Yeah!

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:43.520
Howa Howa

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:44.730
Kira Kira

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:45.680
Yeah! Yeah!

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:48.420
What color is your egg?

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:51.230
Yeah! Yeah! Yeah!

00:01:56.350 --> 00:01:59.020
I see. This is remarkably effective.

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:04.030
I can clearly see how the ? Eggs will cause the Embryo to appear.

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:09.080
The science team will lead the operation this time.

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:09.720
Yes.

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:13.100
And if the Embryo appears...

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:13.720
Ikuto.

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:18.350
I know. I'll make sure I catch it.

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:24.830
Nice working with you. I'm Lulu De Morcerf.

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:25.430
Sure.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:27.550
What's your problem?

00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:28.930
Get off your high horses, y'all!

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:31.510
You're the ones who should get off a horse-nya!

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:34.080
And another thing, saying -nya all the time is my deal-nya!

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:36.840
Naw, not "nya!" It's "y'all," yeah!

00:02:39.460 --> 00:02:44.510
Let Your Singing Heart Take Wing!

00:02:39.460 --> 00:02:44.510
Episode 55

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:46.220
It's gotta be meat buns!

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:49.140
No, it should definitely be sweet bean buns.

00:02:49.610 --> 00:02:51.770
You should buy pudding buns.

00:02:52.170 --> 00:02:55.250
Whatever, okay? Just hurry up and decide.

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:04.470
Oh, Senpai! I got the eight sports drinks.

00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:06.800
Okay, I'll be back in a jiffy!

00:03:07.990 --> 00:03:09.400
That song...

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:13.140
Wasn't that "Heartful Song?"

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:15.350
Yeah, yeah! It's Hoshina Utau's!

00:03:15.810 --> 00:03:17.540
Do you like her, too?

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:21.020
Utau-chan is just so great, you know?

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:23.060
She's pretty, and cool.

00:03:23.060 --> 00:03:26.890
Her earlier songs were cool and all, but this new ballad is just the greatest!

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:30.890
It's too bad she hasn't appeared on TV lately, though.

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:33.930
But Utau's still working hard, you know.

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:36.220
She even did a secret impromptu concert in the suburbs.

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:40.210
Are you a friend of hers?

00:03:41.710 --> 00:03:42.720
And if I am?

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:47.510
Really?! Then, could you possibly let me actually <i>meet</i> Utau-chan?

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:50.580
Please! No big deal, right? I'd be so grateful!

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:51.480
But...

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:56.590
Oops, I'm in the middle of a drink run. Okay, it's a promise, right?

00:03:56.590 --> 00:03:58.100
S-Sure.

00:04:01.350 --> 00:04:02.750
What's your name?

00:04:02.750 --> 00:04:04.830
I-I'm Hinamori Amu.

00:04:04.830 --> 00:04:08.340
So you're Amu-chan. I'm Minagawa Hitomi.

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:11.010
Here's my addy. I'll leave the rest up to you!

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:14.690
What a character.

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:16.220
Wait, now what am I going to do?!

00:04:16.220 --> 00:04:18.310
I ended up promising to introduce her!

00:04:18.630 --> 00:04:22.440
And therefore, today will be spicy shrimp chili buns.

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:24.190
It's decided!

00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:26.720
Did you even hear what I just said?

00:04:37.450 --> 00:04:39.420
That there's is darn tasty!

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:42.500
Father, try to restrain the Nagoya accent, shall we?

00:04:42.850 --> 00:04:48.250
I am sorry, my princess. Your mother's cooking is so delicious, I couldn't help myself.

00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:52.790
People who cook for a living don't want to cook themselves at home.

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:57.430
Just like people who are actresses don't want to watch dramas when they're home, either.

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:01.100
But you're watching a variety program.

00:04:59.170 --> 00:05:01.100
Oh? So at home, you...

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:05.100
It's tough being the wife of a French chef.

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:07.560
But I always cheat a little, and make meat and potato stew.

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:12.030
But your meat and potato stew <i>is</i> darn tasty!

00:05:12.030 --> 00:05:13.880
You make me so happy, my honey!

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:14.710
Maman.

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:15.690
Papa.

00:05:15.690 --> 00:05:16.970
Oh, Grandmere!

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:19.900
Maman, please forgive me!

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:21.600
Mother, I'm sorry!

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:24.770
I'm just kidding. Grandmother is in Paris, remember?

00:05:31.340 --> 00:05:37.460
Maman, have you forgotten when you won the best leading actress award?

00:05:37.860 --> 00:05:39.720
She ain't forgot about it!

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:42.640
Isn't she wearing that jewelry you made her again today?

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:44.410
That's true.

00:05:46.810 --> 00:05:56.210
I won this award because of this jewelry. It was made for me by my Lulu, my goddess of good fortune.

00:05:57.480 --> 00:06:01.680
Anyway, we'll get that Embryo all right, for your mama.

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:05.880
And when ya do, she'll be a shoo-in for the best picture award!

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:07.680
Keep it a secret from Easter, okay?

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:12.520
I know, I know! It's a secret just between you 'n me!

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:16.730
Ah, what should I do?

00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:19.280
What should I say when I see Utau?

00:06:19.280 --> 00:06:20.680
Scenario 1!

00:06:20.660 --> 00:06:28.170
Sanjo Productions

00:06:21.070 --> 00:06:24.070
Hey, there's this girl I know who wants to meet you, and...

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:28.180
Why, exactly, do I have to meet your friends?

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:30.420
That's not going to work.

00:06:30.420 --> 00:06:31.930
Scenario 2!

00:06:31.880 --> 00:06:39.840
Sanjo Productions

00:06:32.330 --> 00:06:35.450
Some girl wants to meet you! Here!

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:36.690
I'm Hitomi!

00:06:36.690 --> 00:06:37.880
Go right ahead!

00:06:37.880 --> 00:06:39.790
I don't have time for you jokers.

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:42.720
That's not going to work either, is it?

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:47.620
It would've been better to simply not make such promises in the first place.

00:06:47.620 --> 00:06:49.270
Definitely.

00:06:49.480 --> 00:06:50.780
{datte}But...

00:06:50.780 --> 00:06:54.100
But you're really just a pushover, aren't you, Amu-chan?

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:00.310
Amu-chan!

00:07:02.030 --> 00:07:03.590
Hitomi-chan!

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:10.550
Hey, did you ask Utau-chan about what we talked about yesterday?

00:07:10.550 --> 00:07:11.710
Um...

00:07:11.710 --> 00:07:15.720
Yeah, today wouldn't be possible, would it?

00:07:16.170 --> 00:07:18.580
Ah, I can hardly wait.

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:21.470
Hitomi-chan, isn't tennis practice really hard?

00:07:22.020 --> 00:07:24.260
She's trying to change the subject.

00:07:24.260 --> 00:07:25.720
What are you doing?

00:07:26.430 --> 00:07:32.970
Yeah, it can be tough, but when that happens I just listen to Utau-chan's songs and I feel better!

00:07:33.350 --> 00:07:35.670
Yup, Utau-chan is the best!

00:07:35.670 --> 00:07:38.000
Seems to have backfired, eh?

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:42.350
Hey, will you listen to my song?

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:53.140
My heartful song, my heartful song.

00:07:53.140 --> 00:08:07.960
I'll sing forever, and wish for it to reach you.

00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:12.520
Wow! You sound just like Utau!

00:08:12.520 --> 00:08:15.460
Really? Do you think I could make my debut?

00:08:15.460 --> 00:08:16.220
Debut?

00:08:16.450 --> 00:08:21.050
I was thinking I'd ask Utau to listen to me sing when I meet her.

00:08:21.050 --> 00:08:26.960
Oh, right! Will you tell her that a fan of hers wants to become a singer?

00:08:26.960 --> 00:08:30.090
Please? No big deal, right? I'd be so grateful!

00:08:30.090 --> 00:08:31.280
U-Um...

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:34.180
Oh, I need to get back to practice.

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:36.440
See you!

00:08:36.440 --> 00:08:38.180
The same pattern again?

00:08:38.470 --> 00:08:42.330
To put it in sumo terms, she's getting pushed all over the ring!

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:44.140
Even in sumo terms, it's...

00:08:44.710 --> 00:08:46.760
What are you going to do?

00:08:46.760 --> 00:08:50.470
Guess I have no choice. A promise is a promise, right?

00:08:53.140 --> 00:08:54.060
No.

00:08:54.670 --> 00:08:56.410
Isn't there anything...

00:08:58.240 --> 00:09:01.370
If we let one fan do this, there will never be an end to it.

00:09:01.370 --> 00:09:05.600
Futhermore, part of an idol's value is the fact that you can't meet them so easily.

00:09:08.490 --> 00:09:11.390
How can someone let it get so messy?

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:14.340
She's really good at singing.

00:09:14.340 --> 00:09:16.070
So even if she doesn't get to meet Utau,

00:09:16.070 --> 00:09:19.420
if you just hear her sing once, you'll decide to debut her right then!

00:09:19.420 --> 00:09:20.970
Or something.

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:22.140
Debut?

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:30.100
Not possible. She might be very good at singing, but that alone isn't enough.

00:09:30.580 --> 00:09:31.970
What do you mean?

00:09:32.820 --> 00:09:34.500
The problem is her drive.

00:09:34.500 --> 00:09:36.600
She needs a strong will to become a pro.

00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:41.440
Someone who can't even open the door at an agency themselves, who just asks others for help, is no good.

00:09:41.440 --> 00:09:43.850
Ah, but I made a promise and...

00:09:44.150 --> 00:09:47.090
It's just unacceptable to ask others for favors.

00:09:47.500 --> 00:09:51.100
The first time I met Utau, she faced me with these competitive eyes and said:

00:09:51.640 --> 00:09:55.180
If you don't accept me, you'll regret it.

00:09:55.490 --> 00:09:57.840
Yup, that's Utau all right.

00:09:57.840 --> 00:09:58.760
Understood?

00:09:59.940 --> 00:10:02.450
The cleaning is all finished!

00:10:03.400 --> 00:10:06.000
My goodness! Everything is sparkling clean!

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:08.170
Oh, it was nothing.

00:10:08.170 --> 00:10:10.760
It would be quite convenient to have someone like you around.

00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:15.310
Hey, would you be my Guardian Character?

00:10:15.310 --> 00:10:18.600
Don't do it, Su! She'll work you to the bone!

00:10:18.600 --> 00:10:20.640
Clean up after yourself!

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:24.860
I want to be the Guardian Character of a cute girl like Amu-chan!

00:10:24.860 --> 00:10:26.090
What's that supposed to mean?

00:10:26.090 --> 00:10:29.470
I don't want to be some old lady's Guardian Character!

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:36.060
That was scary.

00:10:36.420 --> 00:10:39.670
What am I going to do? What should I say to Hitomi-chan?

00:10:39.670 --> 00:10:40.560
Amu.

00:10:44.990 --> 00:10:46.230
Utau.

00:11:00.520 --> 00:11:01.640
That hit the spot!

00:11:02.010 --> 00:11:05.280
We were just at the office, and it sure was a mess.

00:11:05.280 --> 00:11:07.990
But it's fine now. It just needed a bit of tidying.

00:11:07.990 --> 00:11:10.300
What?! You cleaned it up?

00:11:10.580 --> 00:11:14.600
But it was just getting dirty enough for that lived-in feeling.

00:11:15.050 --> 00:11:19.680
A lived-in feeling? That is a world I do not comprehend.

00:11:20.880 --> 00:11:24.310
You've got to be kidding. Why, exactly, do I have to meet your friends?

00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:27.810
Yup, exactly the response I expected.

00:11:28.390 --> 00:11:30.350
I'm home!

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:40.170
If I do well, maybe I can debut as a singer!

00:11:40.170 --> 00:11:41.640
I can't believe it!

00:11:41.640 --> 00:11:43.600
Maybe I should practice giving out autographs!

00:11:45.650 --> 00:11:48.930
But I want to continue playing tennis, too.

00:11:49.870 --> 00:11:52.090
A tennis player that sings and dances?

00:11:54.530 --> 00:11:56.870
She's a worryin', all right!

00:12:00.430 --> 00:12:04.350
It must be great to be Utau-chan.

00:12:09.110 --> 00:12:11.560
Who are you? Do you want something with me?

00:12:11.980 --> 00:12:15.810
You are lost, aren't you?

00:12:17.630 --> 00:12:19.650
You want to become a tennis player.

00:12:19.650 --> 00:12:21.340
You also want to become a singer.

00:12:21.820 --> 00:12:25.160
No, you want to become Hoshina Utau.

00:12:25.740 --> 00:12:27.000
Become Utau-chan?

00:12:27.390 --> 00:12:32.720
Yes. Become Utau, and let me hear her song.

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:40.100
Will that jewel suffice on its own?

00:12:40.100 --> 00:12:42.310
Chief, look at this!

00:12:48.430 --> 00:12:51.180
It's wait and see-nya.

00:12:52.670 --> 00:12:53.430
Where are you going?

00:12:53.840 --> 00:12:57.470
My lesson. I have to head back to the office and then leave immediately.

00:12:57.760 --> 00:13:01.570
That's a pro for you! Trying hard even when no one's watching!

00:13:01.570 --> 00:13:08.300
She is like a gracefully swimming swan, whose legs are paddling furiously under the surface.

00:13:08.300 --> 00:13:09.010
Paddle, paddle!

00:13:15.790 --> 00:13:18.000
This is magic jewelry.

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:21.690
If you put this on, your dream will come true.

00:13:28.470 --> 00:13:32.890
Just do what y'all wanna do!

00:13:33.140 --> 00:13:35.890
? Character Change.

00:13:37.130 --> 00:13:39.550
Amu-chan, I can sense a ? Egg!

00:13:39.550 --> 00:13:40.560
Again?

00:13:40.560 --> 00:13:43.070
A ? Egg? What's that?

00:13:43.070 --> 00:13:45.050
It's Easter's new plan.

00:13:45.050 --> 00:13:49.310
They forcibly draw out children's hearts' eggs, and make them run wild.

00:13:49.310 --> 00:13:51.060
Utau, come with us.

00:13:51.370 --> 00:13:54.100
Utau has a lesson to attend.

00:13:54.100 --> 00:13:57.060
She doesn't have time to mess around with Easter!

00:13:57.730 --> 00:13:58.800
Utau.

00:13:58.800 --> 00:14:02.280
A song. I can hear a song.

00:14:02.280 --> 00:14:05.270
This song... It's Utau-chan's!

00:14:06.220 --> 00:14:07.460
My song?

00:14:07.460 --> 00:14:09.530
Amu-chan, could it be?

00:14:09.530 --> 00:14:10.260
Yeah.

00:14:10.570 --> 00:14:30.920
Give birth to a new me, have courage, don't be embarrassed.

00:14:18.240 --> 00:14:19.010
What's that?

00:14:22.080 --> 00:14:22.850
Hey!

00:14:30.920 --> 00:14:37.780
My heartful song, my heartful song.

00:14:34.820 --> 00:14:36.390
What spectacular energy!

00:14:36.780 --> 00:14:38.320
Oh, it gets better.

00:14:37.780 --> 00:14:52.330
I'll sing forever, and wish for it to reach you.

00:14:38.320 --> 00:14:41.390
Her dream will run ever wilder.

00:14:43.240 --> 00:14:46.810
I want everyone to hear Utau-chan's song!

00:14:47.550 --> 00:14:53.310
Look! They're all so moved by my singing!

00:14:53.590 --> 00:14:56.300
Manta-kun, how's the data looking?

00:14:55.130 --> 00:15:08.120
Like awakening to the kindness of distant memories

00:14:56.850 --> 00:14:57.520
Huh?

00:14:57.520 --> 00:14:59.230
<i>How is the data?</i>

00:14:59.230 --> 00:15:00.840
<i>Oh! It's-</i>

00:15:02.310 --> 00:15:04.420
What is she doing? Good grief.

00:15:04.420 --> 00:15:05.770
Useless.

00:15:05.770 --> 00:15:06.810
If the Embryo appears...

00:15:08.120 --> 00:15:15.560
I'll become true to myself.

00:15:11.730 --> 00:15:12.640
Hitomi-chan!

00:15:13.110 --> 00:15:15.020
It's Hinamori Amu! Crap!

00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:22.210
My heartful song, my heartful song.

00:15:16.160 --> 00:15:17.180
Utau.

00:15:22.210 --> 00:15:24.760
Don't let the song reach your ears, people!

00:15:22.210 --> 00:15:36.510
I'll sing forever, and wish for it to reach you.

00:15:26.260 --> 00:15:27.510
It's already too late!

00:15:28.110 --> 00:15:29.740
What is the meaning of this?

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:31.310
El's unaffected?

00:15:31.310 --> 00:15:34.880
You're ten years too young to impersonate Utau-chan!

00:15:34.880 --> 00:15:36.510
Oh, she's just not listening.

00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:38.310
Hitomi-chan!

00:15:39.840 --> 00:15:41.430
Utau-chan!

00:15:42.840 --> 00:15:43.800
So that's a ? Egg?

00:15:44.360 --> 00:15:46.750
Your song is amazing, Utau-chan!

00:15:46.750 --> 00:15:49.060
Look at how moved everyone is!

00:15:49.560 --> 00:15:53.830
That's not being moved; that's manipulating their hearts!

00:15:53.830 --> 00:15:56.810
All your singing is doing is binding people's hearts!

00:15:58.060 --> 00:15:59.210
No.

00:15:59.210 --> 00:16:00.280
Utau-chan said...

00:16:00.280 --> 00:16:01.720
My song...

00:16:02.140 --> 00:16:04.470
That can't be!

00:16:05.230 --> 00:16:06.310
What's that?

00:16:17.690 --> 00:16:20.640
Character Transformation: Singer Dream!

00:16:21.030 --> 00:16:22.400
Character Transformation?

00:16:22.400 --> 00:16:24.730
Amu-chan, Character Transform with me!

00:16:24.730 --> 00:16:25.390
Right.

00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:30.310
My heart:

00:16:30.930 --> 00:16:31.970
Unlock!

00:16:50.670 --> 00:16:53.360
Character Transformation: Amulet Spade!

00:16:57.340 --> 00:17:00.390
Heartful Song!

00:17:03.910 --> 00:17:06.180
Colorful Canvas!

00:17:12.100 --> 00:17:13.000
Amu!

00:17:13.800 --> 00:17:17.490
Amazing, isn't it? This is the power of Utau-chan's song!

00:17:21.160 --> 00:17:23.730
Yeah, it's quite mind-boggling.

00:17:24.530 --> 00:17:27.150
Embryo, come on out, y'hear!

00:17:30.260 --> 00:17:33.140
Heartful Song!

00:17:37.440 --> 00:17:40.180
Power is welling up.

00:17:47.700 --> 00:17:50.850
Prism Music!

00:17:56.590 --> 00:17:57.840
Wow!

00:17:57.840 --> 00:17:59.420
Prism Music!

00:18:00.990 --> 00:18:02.920
El, our turn.

00:18:03.350 --> 00:18:03.970
Okay!

00:18:05.050 --> 00:18:06.460
My heart:

00:18:06.460 --> 00:18:07.470
Unlock!

00:18:23.050 --> 00:18:25.630
Character Transformation: Seraphic Charm!

00:18:26.950 --> 00:18:28.140
Utau-chan!

00:18:28.470 --> 00:18:32.390
You over there! Listen well to Utau-chan's song!

00:18:33.710 --> 00:18:36.220
Angel Cradle!

00:18:54.430 --> 00:18:57.540
I'm nothing to compared to the real Utau-chan, after all.

00:19:00.650 --> 00:19:03.460
Hitomi-chan, it's not a competition!

00:19:04.010 --> 00:19:07.460
She's right. You should just sing your own song.

00:19:08.010 --> 00:19:10.340
My own song?

00:19:12.070 --> 00:19:14.640
Negative Heart: Lock On!

00:19:18.290 --> 00:19:20.850
Open Heart!

00:19:45.410 --> 00:19:46.970
It's the Embryo, y'all!

00:19:50.660 --> 00:19:52.280
What? Where?

00:19:52.280 --> 00:19:52.840
Ikuto!

00:19:55.650 --> 00:19:58.350
That darned cat saddled off somewhere!

00:19:58.350 --> 00:19:59.870
Your Nagoya accent...

00:19:59.870 --> 00:20:00.540
Oopsie.

00:20:03.680 --> 00:20:05.090
This is...

00:20:05.090 --> 00:20:06.680
Chief, look at this!

00:20:07.650 --> 00:20:08.980
This waveform...

00:20:09.490 --> 00:20:15.610
Oh, I see! With this data, that plan might actually work!

00:20:15.610 --> 00:20:16.910
Exactly!

00:20:16.910 --> 00:20:18.180
I get it!

00:20:18.180 --> 00:20:19.530
Do you really?

00:20:19.530 --> 00:20:20.450
Uh...

00:20:21.520 --> 00:20:23.510
Hitomi-chan, are you okay?

00:20:25.250 --> 00:20:27.950
Huh? Amu-chan?

00:20:29.690 --> 00:20:31.390
Utau-chan?

00:20:32.540 --> 00:20:34.670
Wow, you're for real!

00:20:35.320 --> 00:20:41.720
But even though I finally get to meet you, it's kind of painful.

00:20:43.140 --> 00:20:46.240
Your singing wasn't bad.

00:20:47.190 --> 00:20:52.340
Acting like you're singing from the heart is just acting, though.

00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:55.840
But I want to be just like you.

00:20:56.840 --> 00:21:00.100
Everyone has their own song in their heart.

00:21:01.030 --> 00:21:02.600
Their own song?

00:21:03.390 --> 00:21:07.060
That's right. I'm sure your song is there somewhere, Hitomi-chan.

00:21:08.770 --> 00:21:11.780
You're right. I'll have to look for it.

00:21:11.780 --> 00:21:13.270
My own song.

00:21:14.030 --> 00:21:17.220
And then, one day, I'll stand on the same stage as you, Utau-chan!

00:21:18.260 --> 00:21:19.850
I can't wait.

00:21:19.850 --> 00:21:22.450
You're just so cool, Utau-chan!

00:21:22.450 --> 00:21:23.640
All right, I'm going for it!

00:21:25.050 --> 00:21:26.880
What happened?

00:21:26.880 --> 00:21:29.790
Everything seems to have resolved itself on its own.

00:21:30.720 --> 00:21:33.770
Jeez, being entranced by some other kid's song.

00:21:33.770 --> 00:21:37.880
I cannot <i>believe</i> you're one of Utau-chan's Guardian Characters!

00:21:37.880 --> 00:21:41.880
Shut up! Coming from you, that really pisses me off!

00:21:41.880 --> 00:21:43.840
Damn You Kick!

00:21:43.840 --> 00:21:45.100
Sheesh.

00:21:46.920 --> 00:21:48.340
You okay with this?

00:21:48.340 --> 00:21:50.310
They'll bark about it later.

00:21:50.310 --> 00:21:51.950
I don't care.

00:22:04.870 --> 00:22:06.170
What is it-nya?

00:22:07.290 --> 00:22:10.150
My violin is gone.

00:22:22.870 --> 00:22:23.370
(For real?)

00:22:25.600 --> 00:22:26.110
(Eh?)

00:22:26.110 --> 00:22:28.320
Lotta love! Lotta love! Lotta love!

00:22:28.800 --> 00:22:31.040
Lotta love! Lotta love! Lotta love!

00:22:31.580 --> 00:22:36.520
If we ended up becoming adults today, {kyou mo}

00:22:36.520 --> 00:22:41.150
I bet we'd lose sight of everything except what's in front of us. {kitto}

00:22:41.150 --> 00:22:42.490
Lotta love! Lotta love!

00:22:42.490 --> 00:22:47.420
So I wonder what we've been {kyoumade}

00:22:47.420 --> 00:22:52.060
so engrossed with finding all this time. {honto}

00:22:52.060 --> 00:22:53.320
Lotta love! Lotta love!

00:22:53.320 --> 00:22:55.050
Someone once said: {dare ga}

00:22:55.050 --> 00:22:57.960
"We were born to be happy, {shiawase}

00:22:57.960 --> 00:23:03.920
so let's live to make others happy!" {soshite}

00:23:05.550 --> 00:23:06.700
How long will I have to  {dore kurai}

00:23:06.700 --> 00:23:08.400
carry all this love in my heart?  {mune ippai}

00:23:08.400 --> 00:23:09.450
How long will I have to {dore kurai}

00:23:09.450 --> 00:23:11.070
carry all this love in my heart?  {mune ippai}

00:23:11.070 --> 00:23:16.580
I wonder when I'll be able to let it all out. {kakaetara}

00:23:16.580 --> 00:23:17.580
How many of {dore kurai}

00:23:17.580 --> 00:23:19.230
all those days in my heart...  {mune ippai}

00:23:19.230 --> 00:23:20.290
How many of{dore kurai}

00:23:20.290 --> 00:23:22.050
all those days in my heart...  {mune ippai}

00:23:22.050 --> 00:23:27.460
How many of them have we run through? {ano hi}

00:23:27.460 --> 00:23:28.510
With this much love {kore kurai}

00:23:28.510 --> 00:23:30.200
filling my heart...  {mune ippai}

00:23:30.200 --> 00:23:31.290
With this much love{kore kurai}

00:23:31.290 --> 00:23:32.870
filling my heart... {mune ippai}

00:23:32.870 --> 00:23:35.590
I hugged you tightly, {kimi wo}

00:23:35.590 --> 00:23:41.130
and during that time, we both felt so much happiness. {futari}

00:23:41.130 --> 00:23:43.310
Lotta love! Lotta love! Lotta love!

00:23:43.310 --> 00:23:43.810
(Why?)

00:23:43.810 --> 00:23:46.000
Lotta love! Lotta love! Lotta love!

00:23:46.530 --> 00:23:48.800
Lotta love! Lotta love! Lotta love!

00:23:49.080 --> 00:23:50.110
(Phew...)

00:23:50.650 --> 00:23:52.040
Amu-chan, did you know?

00:23:52.040 --> 00:23:54.250
There's a new Jack!

00:23:54.250 --> 00:23:56.080
Huh? A new Jack?

00:23:56.080 --> 00:24:00.230
We're gaining another friend at Seiyo Academy.

00:24:00.230 --> 00:24:01.480
